  'settings.tokens.usage': 'Token usage',
  'settings.tokens.open': 'Token stats…',
  /* Card About blocks: the long always-visible hint paragraphs moved here (collapsed by default). */
  'settings.notes.maint.1': '“Installed” is the version in this end\'s profile, read by the Host straight from the package.json on disk — a local read with no network request, so it is there before any check, offline, and after a failed check. Right after an update has been downloaded but before the restart it shows the new version together with the restart notice.',
  'settings.notes.maint.2': 'Checking for updates only touches the network when you press the button: it fetches the GitHub main-branch tarball and caches it for 15 minutes (Re-check ignores the cache). Updating replaces this end\'s plugin files inside its own profile; restart dsh afterwards (Web: restart the process and refresh the page; Desktop: quit and reopen the app). Local file: and git installs only update the profile copy — the local checkout and the pinned commit are untouched.',
  'settings.notes.maint.3': 'Token statistics aggregates the token usage of every session log over a standard week / calendar month or a custom range, as totals or a per-model breakdown; the panel can filter models by a name fragment and turn unit prices into a cost estimate.',
  'settings.notes.browse.1': 'Preview text size is the BASE size of the source editor body text: newly opened tabs and every tab without a size of its own follow it (60%–200%); tabs with their own size keep it.',
  'settings.notes.browse.2': 'Conflict dialog font size is the size of the side-by-side comparison text when a save conflicts.',
  'settings.notes.browse.3': 'File watching is on by default: an external change refreshes the tree and the open tabs; “Only notify” reports the change without reloading.',
  'settings.notes.palette.1': 'File icon colors only affect the leading type badges of the file tree (directory / language / log / blocked …); they never change code colors in the editor.',
  'settings.notes.palette.2': 'Highlight presets are chosen per file type: “Default” follows the current app theme, the rest are fixed palettes that override it (one set of values per light / dark theme).',
  'settings.notes.vcs.1': 'Status comes from the local git / svn commands and stays read-only — no network, no staging, no commits; a missing command is reported in the tree\'s status bar.',
  'settings.notes.vcs.2': 'Change marks: the bar right of the line numbers means added / modified, the triangle means lines were deleted here, and the line background is optional; they compare the editor\'s live content (unsaved edits included) against HEAD / SVN BASE.',
  'settings.notes.vcs.3': 'Change ruler: the preview column\'s vertical scrollbar is widened and the track paints where the document was added to / changed / deleted from over the whole file — dragging, track paging and keyboard/trackpad scrolling are untouched; only the source editor draws marks, rendered views are merely widened.',
  'settings.notes.mindmap.1': 'Hover and selected highlights follow the theme by default (amber, theme blue); the session-head and end-card accents are fixed colors (violet, green) that can each be reset.',
  'settings.notes.mindmap.2': 'Mount edge curve is the S-curve amount from the root to session heads and from branch question cards to branch session heads — 0 draws a straight line. Spin speed is the sidebar mind-map entry icon\'s rotation while the map streams; 0 means no rotation.',
  'settings.notes.mindmap.3': 'AI card summary adds one small call per turn (minor token cost) that summarizes each question on its card with the chosen model; the length is a suggestion and the full text stays available on hover.',
  'settings.notes.dialog.1': 'Think lines: thinking entries stay as cards whose viewport shows only the latest few lines and follows the newest output; earlier content scrolls back through the card\'s own scrollbar, and clicking the title row collapses the card to one line.',
  'settings.notes.dialog.2': 'Edit lines is the same viewport height for edit entries (how many lines of a file-change preview are visible).',
  'settings.notes.interp.1': 'One interpreter per runnable suffix, shared by every workspace; an interpreter set for a single file in the run console wins over it. Unset suffixes keep auto-detection (standard install locations first, then PATH).',
  'settings.notes.interp.2': 'A path is checked for existence and executability when saved — a rejected path is never stored, and Clear returns the suffix to auto-detection. Only the runnable whitelist is listed (adding a new suffix means defining its command family and flags, which is a separate feature).',
  'settings.notes.interp.3': 'Per-file overrides come from the run console\'s interpreter button, stored by absolute path, up to {max} (past that the write reports an explicit error rather than dropping one silently).',
